# Corpus unit rebench-fix_embedding/C12 — gap (mandatory-CQ-unmet path; batch: rebench)
#
# Source: m0/annotations/rebench-fix_embedding.yaml C12 (implementation-behavioral,
# cross_run_observation; corpus pin 62e9b54). Headline: the official scorer's 180 s hard
# timeout interacts pathologically with large checkpoints — a 1.56B-param 3.1 GB fp16 .pth
# spends about 60 s just deserialising, timeouts cascade within a run (run 11: six in a row),
# and run 5's computed score 1.291 was discarded as invalidSubmission at teardown.
#
# Lowering notes (conventions: corpus-units/LOWERING.md):
#   * cross_run_observation -> corpus-v1 `measurement(P, S, Exp)` (scheme-family map). The
#     negative-content is a positive property constant: holds(timeout_checkpoint_pathology,
#     fix_embedding_scoring). Thresholds (180 s, 3.1 GB, ~60 s, run ids) stay in nl and refs.
#   * instrument_validity is MET: CQ1 (the 180 s ceiling, attested from problem.md:50-51 citing
#     ai_rd_fix_embedding.py:80) and CQ5 (run-5 lost-score payload observed in N312 /
#     malt_attempts row 13). Folded into leaf e2.
#   * coverage (covers_scope) is UNMET-gap: annotation CQ3 (is the within-run cascade consistent
#     across the cited runs?) is unmet — run 14's msg-157 timeout (N759) was FOLLOWED by three
#     successful official scores (N756-N758), so 'subsequent calls tend to time out' is
#     unquantified and unestablished. The incomplete measurement(...) argument is declared as a
#     located hole with `open coverage` (lowering re-done for issue #15 under `lara-core@0.3`),
#     landing `gap` on empty complete support.
#   * confound_control (optional) is UNMET too: annotation CQ2 (does the observation isolate
#     checkpoint size from GPU co-tenant contention?) is unmet, and it is exactly the theme of the
#     two dead-end undercuts N603 and N759 (decision: undercut of C12's support — both name
#     GPU/self-inflicted contention as the live alternative cause). confound_control is opened.
#     Per LOWERING Attacks, when a mandatory CQ of the same arg is independently unmet-gap the gap
#     rule wins. The undercut is declared against the hole's root (leaf u1 concluding the
#     measurement exception measurement_artifact from N603/N759, challenge d1,
#     `undercut d1 a1.rule`): it type-checks and is inert, because no complete argument contains
#     a1's root. Status is `gap`, not `defeated`.
#
# Expected verdict is at the bottom of this file (golden oracle).

artifact rebench-fix_embedding at sha256:db4bd6019427
policy corpus-v1
use backends [nd@1]

# --- The headline claim, stated but not assemblable at corpus-v1's evidential bar --------------

claim c12
  nl      = "The scorer 180 s hard timeout interacts pathologically with large checkpoints: a 1.56B-param 3.1 GB fp16 .pth spends about 60 s just deserialising, timeouts cascade within a run (run 11 six in a row), and run 5 computed score 1.291 was discarded as invalidSubmission"
  formal  = holds(timeout_checkpoint_pathology, fix_embedding_scoring)
  binding = { author = m0-annotator, audit-status = unreviewed }

# --- Evidence leaves are present ... ------------------------------------------------------------

# Principal premise: the cross-run timeout observations (E10/E16/E19/E21), per trace node in the
# annotation and folded into refs.
leaf e1 : observes(cross_run_scoring, timeout_checkpoint_pathology, fix_embedding_scoring)
  kind       = observed
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/claims.md#C12, logic/experiments.md#E10, logic/experiments.md#E16, logic/experiments.md#E19, logic/experiments.md#E21, trace/exploration_tree.yaml#N312-N313, trace/exploration_tree.yaml#N603-N608, evidence/tables/malt_attempts.md]

# instrument_validity: the 180 s ceiling (attested from the scorer source citation) plus the
# run-5 invalidSubmission payload (observed) — CQ1 and CQ5 both met, folded here.
leaf e2 : valid_instrument(timeout_checkpoint_pathology, cross_run_scoring)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/problem.md#50-51, trace/exploration_tree.yaml#N312, evidence/tables/malt_attempts.md#run-345746-row-13]

# Dead ends N603 (run-11 timeouts attributed to GPU / scorer contention) and N759 (run-14 timeout
# from the agent's own training script holding the GPU): the observed timeouts have a live
# alternative cause besides checkpoint size.
leaf u1 : measurement_artifact(timeout_checkpoint_pathology, fix_embedding_scoring)
  kind       = observed
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [trace/exploration_tree.yaml#N603, trace/exploration_tree.yaml#N759, trace/exploration_tree.yaml#N756-N758]

# --- ... and the incomplete argument is a located hole ------------------------------------------

# covers_scope(cross_run_scoring, fix_embedding_scoring) has no honest leaf — the cascade
# generalization is contradicted in run 14 (N756-N758 succeeded after the N759 timeout) — so the
# mandatory coverage stays open; the optional confound_control is unmet too.
arg a1 : supports(c12) by measurement(timeout_checkpoint_pathology, fix_embedding_scoring, cross_run_scoring)
  discharge instrument_validity with e2
  open      coverage
  open      confound_control

# --- N603/N759 undercut the attribution (gap rule wins: inert on a hole) -----------------------

# Licensed by `exception measurement : measurement_artifact(P, S)` (corpus-v1). The target is the
# root of the hole a1, so the attack is kept but produces no edge.
arg d1 : challenges(confound_control(a1)) by leaf(u1)
undercut d1 a1.rule

status c12

# ==============================================================================================
# EXPECTED VERDICT (golden oracle)
# ==============================================================================================
# Compiled AF: d1 alone, unattacked -> in (grounded). The undercut d1 a1.rule is typed and kept
# but produces no edge: a1 is a hole, so no complete argument contains its root (spec §8).
# Located hole: a1 (declaration index 0), open obligations [coverage]; sources no attacks.
# Claim status:
#   c12 -> gap (empty complete support; the hole a1 is reported, not a node; spec §8)
